draw(rightanglemark(C,P,H,3.5));

draw(rightanglemark(H,Q,C,3.5));

[/asy]

$\angle AHB = \angle DHE$이며, 사각형 $CDHE$에서, 
\[
\angle DHE = 360^\circ - \angle HEC - \angle ECD - \angle CDH
\]
따라서,
\[
\angle DHE = 360^\circ - 90^\circ - \angle ACB - 90^\circ
\]
\[
\angle DHE = 180^\circ - \angle ACB
\]
이다. 

$\triangle ABC$에서, $180^\circ - \angle ACB = \angle BAC + \angle ABC = 54^\circ + 52^\circ = \boxed{106^\circ}$.

We have that $r = \sqrt{0^2 + 3^2} = 3.$  Also, if we draw the line connecting the origin and $(0,3),$ this line makes an angle of $\frac{\pi}{2}$ with the positive $x$-axis.

